{"ref":"BDB, שׁוֹבֵב","hw":"שׁוֹבֵב","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">שׁוֹבֵב</span></big>  <strong>adj. backturning, apostate (</strong>perhaps for <span dir=\"rtl\">מְשׁוֹ׳</span>, v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, שׁוֹבָב\" href=\"/BDB,_שׁוֹבָב\", dir=\"rtl\">i. שׁוֹבָב</a><strong>)</strong>;—as subst., <span dir=\"rtl\">לְשׁו׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Micah 2:4\" href=\"/Micah.2.4\">Mi 2:4</a> (but read prob. <span dir=\"rtl\">שׁוֹבֵינוּ</span> <em>our captors</em>); f. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַבַּת הַשּׁוֹבֵבָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 31:22\" href=\"/Jeremiah.31.22\">Je 31:22</a> (of Israel), <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 49:4\" href=\"/Jeremiah.49.4\">49:4</a> (of Ammon).","next":"BDB, יָשׁוּב²","prev":"BDB, שׁוֹבָב²"}